Here's a simple example of a brute force algorithm in JavaScript that attempts to guess a 4-digit PIN code. This is purely for educational purposes, and you should never use brute force to access systems without permission.

```javascript
function bruteForcePin(pin) {
  const possibleDigits = '0123456789';
  let attempts = 0;

  for (let i = 0; i < possibleDigits.length; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < possibleDigits.length; j++) {
      for (let k = 0; k < possibleDigits.length; k++) {
        for (let l = 0; l < possibleDigits.length; l++) {
