```

In this example, the `bruteForcePin` function generates all possible 4-digit combinations from the digits 0-9 and compares each one to the target PIN. If a match is found, it prints the found PIN and the number of attempts it took. If no match is found after all combinations are tried, it prints a message indicating the PIN was not found.

Keep in mind that brute force methods are generally inefficient and can take a very long time to find a solution, especially as the complexity of the problem increases. They are also not recommended for real-world applications where security is a concern. Always use secure and ethical coding practices.

